    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG are pleased to introduce No. 76 Saint Maelruan's Park to the market. Extended to the side to incorporate a downstairs bedroom with ensuite shower room, and offering generous living accommodation extending to a spacious 114 sqm (approx.), this four-bedroom family home is tucked away in the sought-after, family-friendly Saint Maelruan's estate. Beautifully maintained and upgraded by the current owners, No. 76 offers well-planned accommodation with a versatility that will appeal to families at every stage. \n\nOn entering through the porch, the care and attention lavished on the home is immediately apparent. The recently refurbished and upgraded kitchen/dining room is positioned to the front and leads through to a rear hall with access to the garden and the versatile fourth bedroom. Currently used as a guest bedroom/home office, this excellent additional space could equally serve as a playroom, den or teenage retreat, depending on the needs of the family. The main hallway leads to the comfortable family living room, with utility area off and sliding doors opening directly onto the rear garden. \n\nThe sunny rear garden is a wonderful extension of the living space, featuring a southerly aspect, astro-turf, paved patio areas and raised beds, creating an ideal setting for children to play and for outdoor entertaining. Upstairs are three generous bedrooms and a recently renovated family bathroom. To the front, the large driveway provides off-street parking for three or more cars.\n\nSaint Maelruan's Park is a particularly appealing setting for young families, with its own national primary school and a strong sense of community within the estate. Tallaght Village is within easy walking distance and offers an extensive range of shops, cafés, restaurants and everyday amenities. The property is also ideally positioned for access to the M50, N7 and N81, while public transport is well catered for with the nearby LUAS Red Line and numerous bus services providing convenient access to Dublin City Centre. With its generous accommodation, excellent outdoor space and highly adaptable layout, No. 76 offers a superb family home with the flexibility to evolve as family life changes."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nPlease see 3D Tour - \nhttps://my.matterport.com/show/?m=Qf3gGuD81v4\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Substantial 4 bed/ 2 bath family home, offering 114sqm (approx.) living accommodation</li><li> GFCH</li><li> Double glazed windows throughout</li><li> Recently renovated kitchen and bathroom</li><li> Sunny rear garden with southerly aspect</li><li> Off-street parking for multiple cars to front</li><li> Tallaght Village is within easy walking distance</li><li> Ideally positioned for access to the M50, N7 and N81</ul>"
      },
